{"parentUuid":"fb3a9c61-eef5-4ca3-8b1f-cfae2280dd6f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DNcjvuf7fbqLuDocumFeZ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TudFQNsuptwvEagdETkghK","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Huub solver Dekker Monash CP 2026 Python binding circuit propagator"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16071,"cache_read_input_tokens":11009,"output_tokens":258,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16071},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":11009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16071,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cassa5oBXdFEdouaFR5Yv","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c4af703-d810-43ad-a6c5-33f02f7b9ec8","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:04.277Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"22334bbd-abb5-4e6d-bf05-dd7129a743ae","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015J29p1xJ86cRroEbHurv1Y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Pumpkin Rust constraint solver LCG GitHub 2026 Python binding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin: A Lazy Clause Generation Constraint Programming solver written in Rust. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin\"},{\"title\":\"pumpkin_solver - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/pumpkin-solver\"},{\"title\":\"ConSoL Lab · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ConSol-Lab\"},{\"title\":\"Pumpkin/pumpkin-solver/src/propagators/element.rs at main · ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin/blob/main/pumpkin-solver/src/propagators/element.rs\"},{\"title\":\"constraint-satisfaction-problem · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/constraint-satisfaction-problem\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ptal/pcp: Constraint programming in Rust · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ptal/pcp\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - rust-or/good_lp: Linear Programming for Rust, with a user-friendly API. This crate allows modeling LP problems, and lets you solve them with various solvers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rust-or/good_lp\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - rust-or/rust-lp-modeler: Lp modeler written in Rust · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rust-or/rust-lp-modeler\"},{\"title\":\"constraint-solver · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/constraint-solver\"},{\"title\":\"constraint-programming · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/constraint-programming?o=desc\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Pumpkin:\n\nPumpkin is a combinatorial optimisation solver developed by the ConSol Lab at TU Delft, based on the lazy clause generation (LCG) constraint programming paradigm. The solver is written in pure Rust, and the project is hosted on GitHub at the ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin repository.\n\nRegarding Python bindings, the python bindings contained in pumpkin-solver-py define the python interface for Pumpkin.\n\nThe search results also reference a 2026 publication: a paper titled 'Using Certifying Constraint Solvers for Generating Step-wise Explanations' was published in the Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence in March 2026.\n\nYou can find the main project repository at https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin and explore the Python bindings through the documentation and examples provided there.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fefc6bae-b9b8-4746-b67b-040addc5446d","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:08.360Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"22334bbd-abb5-4e6d-bf05-dd7129a743ae","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fb3a9c61-eef5-4ca3-8b1f-cfae2280dd6f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JdrtQcJt6vjaiovqXWxAmr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Glasgow Constraint Solver ciaranm 2026 propagator update\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver: A constraint programming solver with support for proof logging · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ciaranm/glasgow-subgraph-solver: A solver for subgraph isomorphism problems, based upon a series of papers by subsets of McCreesh, Prosser, and Trimble. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-subgraph-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Ciaran McCreesh\",\"url\":\"https://ciaranm.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-51372-6_19\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard\",\"url\":\"https://ciaranm.github.io/papers/icgt2020-glasgow-subgraph-solver.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7314700/\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/The-Glasgow-Subgraph-Solver:-Using-Constraint-to-McCreesh-Prosser/d25dccef7e17f0af733509377f577390f0933a3b\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver/releases\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver Ciaran McCreesh Patrick Prosser James Trimble\",\"url\":\"https://www.dcs.gla.ac.uk/~ciaran/talks/2020-06-icgt-gss.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/342441551_The_Glasgow_Subgraph_Solver_Using_Constraint_Programming_to_Tackle_Hard_Subgraph_Isomorphism_Problem_Variants\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the Glasgow Constraint Solver and updates related to Ciaran McCreesh's work:\n\nThe Glasgow Constraint Solver is a new project that brings proof logging to constraint programming. The project is maintained by Ciaran McCreesh on GitHub at https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver.\n\nRegarding recent 2026 updates: A paper titled \"Faster Certified Symmetry Breaking using Orders with Auxiliary Variables\" by Markus Anders, Bart Bogaerts, Benjamin Bogø, Arthur Gontier, Wietze Koops, Ciaran McCreesh, and others is scheduled for publication at AAAI 2026.\n\nThe solver's architecture involves propagators that perform constraint solving work. Each constraint is associated with zero or more propagators, which do the actual work. A propagator is always called at least once, at the root node, and after that, it is only called when triggered by an event.\n\nThe search results show recent releases and publications related to proof logging for various constraints, with the most recent being AAAI 2025 work on integer multiplication constraint propagation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9640e986-369e-4ac5-b656-2b69e9456883","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:10.754Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fb3a9c61-eef5-4ca3-8b1f-cfae2280dd6f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9c4af703-d810-43ad-a6c5-33f02f7b9ec8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TudFQNsuptwvEagdETkghK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Huub solver Dekker Monash CP 2026 Python binding circuit propagator\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - huub-solver/huub: CP+SAT solver framework built to be reliable, performant, and extensible · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/huub-solver/huub\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG Jip J. Dekker #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Jip Dekker - Monash University\",\"url\":\"https://research.monash.edu/en/persons/jip-dekker/\"},{\"title\":\"Monash Bioinformatics Platform · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MonashBioinformaticsPlatform?language=python\"},{\"title\":\"Projects - Jip J. Dekker\",\"url\":\"https://dekker.one/projects/\"},{\"title\":\"custom propagator needed ? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3303\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3303\"},{\"title\":\"ITI9136 - Algorithms and programming foundations in Python - Monash University\",\"url\":\"https://handbook.monash.edu/2021/units/ITI9136\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/extra-require/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - yongdd/langevin-fts: Polymer Field Theory Simulations with Python\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yongdd/langevin-fts\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - duasfl8r/propagator.py: A propagator network in Python, inspired by Radul & Sussman's The Art of the Propagator\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/duasfl8r/propagator.py\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about Huub and some related work:\n\nHuub is a reliable CP+SAT solver that combines strong propagation with modern solving techniques to deliver competitive performance on demanding decision problems, and you can add your own propagators, branchers, and even replace the underlying SAT solver.\n\nThe project is authored by Dekker, Jip J. and Stuckey, Peter J., and Jip Dekker is an early-career researcher at Monash University in optimization.\n\nThe search results also show a 2025 CP conference paper authored by Jip J. Dekker on \"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG,\" which discusses Huub as an LCG solver built based on the IPASIR-UP interface to SAT engines, with a modular design that allows swapping in any SAT solver that supports the interface.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about Python bindings, circuit propagators, or the \"CP 2026\" context you mentioned. If you're looking for more specific information about those features, you might want to check the official Huub GitHub repository or related documentation directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5c3eb76d-7aa2-487a-aacf-57fe7875e1a8","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:12.734Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9c4af703-d810-43ad-a6c5-33f02f7b9ec8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
