{"parentUuid":"f153ad5c-7a22-4db0-9b03-3aed550068d5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011b6HXhEhdFYNhveHw6BBQm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018dcQDGy1xC7ihQF4vZqaUf","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/huub-solver/huub","prompt":"Latest commit date, releases, README content. Python binding status, implemented propagators (especially circuit, cumulative, no_overlap_2d, element, table, flow), how to use it (FlatZinc only or also Python API), project activity in 2025-2026."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3816,"cache_read_input_tokens":27080,"output_tokens":554,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3816},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":27080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3816,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cassb7dqjYBNuLWTPe9qA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc683276-3b6a-44d3-9971-00e93b367f39","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:21.338Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"04739dd3-bcc0-41c1-9cd9-94fd0a3c20ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X7EqrGooc1WzoZfxJ72Z2n","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pumpkin: A Constraint Programming Solver in Rust\n\n## Project Overview\nPumpkin is a combinatorial optimization solver developed by ConSol Lab at TU Delft, based on lazy clause generation constraint programming. The project emphasizes efficiency, usability, and documentation while being written in pure Rust.\n\n## Key Features & Recent Achievements\n- **2025 MiniZinc Challenge**: Won bronze medal in the fixed search track\n- **Proof Logging**: Can generate certificates of unsatisfiability (detailed in CP'24 paper)\n- **Active Development**: 594 commits with latest release (pumpkin-solver-v0.3.0) in February 2026\n\n## Supported Constraints\nThe solver implements:\n- Cumulative and disjunctive global constraints\n- Element constraint\n- Arithmetic operations (linear inequalities, division, multiplication, maximum, absolute value)\n- Clausal constraints\n\n## Python Bindings Status\nThe repository includes `pumpkin-solver-py` as a component, providing Python interface access to the solver alongside Rust library and CLI implementations.\n\n## Installation & Usage\nAvailable via:\n- Cargo: `cargo add pumpkin-solver` (library) or `cargo install pumpkin-solver` (CLI)\n- PyPI: `pumpkin-solver` package\n- MiniZinc backend integration supported\n\n## Development\nThe project encourages contributions with emphasis on documentation and code quality, using pre-commit hooks and nightly Rust formatting standards. Primary language composition: 90.8% Rust, with supporting C, C++, MiniZinc, and Python components."}]},"uuid":"5371f2a0-3483-4fce-bf79-34294d7141fc","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:25.246Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"04739dd3-bcc0-41c1-9cd9-94fd0a3c20ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f153ad5c-7a22-4db0-9b03-3aed550068d5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pic4WcDP1i1PNebaF2Wijs","type":"tool_result","content":"# Glasgow Constraint Solver Overview\n\n## Project Status\nThe Glasgow Constraint Solver is a work-in-progress constraint programming system developed by Ciaran McCreesh. It features \"no stable API or design\" currently, though the existing code is largely functional.\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Proof Logging**: The solver's distinguishing capability is generating verifiable proofs in VeriPB 3.0 format. As the documentation states: \"The solver converts the high level constraint problem given into a low-level pseudo-Boolean model\" for proof verification purposes.\n\n**Multi-Frontend Support**: \n- XCSP3 solver with full XCSP3-core (v3.2) constraint vocabulary\n- MiniZinc frontend (more limited, relying on stdlib decomposition)\n- C++ API for manual problem specification\n\n## Technical Requirements\n- C++23 compiler (GCC 13+ or Clang 21+)\n- CMake 3.21+\n- Optional: VeriPB for proof verification, libxml2 for XCSP, MiniZinc tools\n\n## Current Development\nThe repository shows active maintenance with 1,263 commits on main. Three build configurations are supported: release (optimized), debug, and sanitized builds with AddressSanitizer/UBSan. The codebase is primarily C++ (93.8%), with supporting CMake and Python components.\n\n## Testing & Verification\nThe project emphasizes correctness through proof logging rather than conventional testing alone, reducing verification burden to trusting the OPB encoding and the VeriPB checker."}]},"uuid":"bf3c411c-9f82-4c87-8732-7c1ec3121697","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:26.657Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f153ad5c-7a22-4db0-9b03-3aed550068d5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cc683276-3b6a-44d3-9971-00e93b367f39","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"adee29cf670b5c3dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018dcQDGy1xC7ihQF4vZqaUf","type":"tool_result","content":"# Huub: CP+SAT Solver Framework\n\n## Overview\nHuub is a Rust-based constraint programming and Boolean satisfiability solver designed for optimization and decision-making systems. The project emphasizes three core qualities: reliability through rigorous testing and safe implementation, performance via strong propagation and modern techniques, and extensibility through customizable propagators and branchers.\n\n## Key Details\n\n**Repository Stats:**\n- 31 stars, 9 forks, 4 issues\n- 384 commits on develop branch\n- Written primarily in Rust (98.1%)\n- MPL-2.0 license\n\n**Core Capabilities:**\nThe framework combines \"the modelling strengths of constraint programming (CP) with the learning and proof machinery of Boolean satisfiability (SAT) solving.\"\n\n**Availability:**\n- Website: huub.solutions\n- Published on crates.io and docs.rs\n- FlatZinc support mentioned via MiniZinc integration\n\n## Current Status\nThe page content doesn't explicitly detail 2025-2026 activity levels, specific Python binding status, or comprehensive lists of implemented propagators. The README references contributors and funding partners but specifics aren't included in the provided excerpt.\n\n**Citation:** The project provides an official software citation with DOI 10.5281/zenodo.15591852 for academic references."}]},"uuid":"5e2d7732-13b5-44cf-a6c3-3b5af72949fe","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:26.860Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc683276-3b6a-44d3-9971-00e93b367f39","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
